---
// ============================================================
// /contact/ — how to reach him.
//
// No contact form. A form needs a server to receive what it
// sends, and this site does not have one. An email address works
// everywhere, needs nothing, and cannot break.
// ============================================================

import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contact"
  description="How to reach Anupam Kumar, and what is most useful to write about."
>
  <article class="prose" data-pagefind-body>
    <h1>Contact</h1>

    <p>
      Email is best:
      <a href="mailto:hello@anupamkumar.org">hello@anupamkumar.org</a>
    </p>

    <p>
      To follow the writing by email, subscribe to
      <a href="https://asranupam.substack.com">the newsletter</a>. To follow it
      in a reader, use <a href="/rss.xml">the RSS feed</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Particularly useful to hear about</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>A figure that looks wrong.</strong> Say which piece or dataset,
        and what you expected instead. On a site whose whole claim is provenance,
        a correction is a contribution.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A dataset that is painful to use.</strong> If the raw source is
        public but unusable, that gap is exactly what this site exists to close.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A source that has moved.</strong> Government links rot
        constantly. If one here leads nowhere, telling me is a real help.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Something that does not work.</strong> A page that scrolls
        sideways on your phone, a tool that will not open, text you cannot read.
        Say what device and browser you were using.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>On reuse</h2>

    <p>
      You do not need permission to reuse the writing or the data — both are
      published under
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>, so
      credit is all that is asked. If you would like a citation in a particular
      format, or the underlying files in a different one, write and ask.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
